WEBVTT

00:04.750 --> 00:06.360
Okay, good.

00:11.540 --> 00:13.650
Hey, could we try recording that again?

00:15.740 --> 00:20.150
Hey, wait! Don't you agree what
we just sang was lacking something?

00:20.900 --> 00:22.310
Shut up.

00:22.310 --> 00:25.250
It's good enough for
a song I'm singing with you.

00:25.910 --> 00:27.130
Good enough?

00:27.600 --> 00:30.850
Do you have any idea how
important this duet project is?

00:30.850 --> 00:34.730
You haven't been trying at all since we
started practicing! What's your problem?

00:34.730 --> 00:38.510
I was looking forward to singing
with Hyuga-sensei's younger brother!

00:44.100 --> 00:46.090
I'm not his brother.

00:46.090 --> 00:48.270
I'm Hyuga Yamato!

00:48.860 --> 00:50.930
S-Stop, guys.

00:50.930 --> 00:52.610
Syo-kun, are you okay?

00:52.610 --> 00:53.950
Yeah.

00:53.950 --> 00:55.530
You just watch.

00:55.530 --> 01:00.890
At the next <i>Muscle Fight</i>,
I'll take down Hyuga Ryuya!

01:06.290 --> 01:08.030
What's his problem?

02:52.540 --> 02:54.970
Good enough?

02:54.970 --> 02:58.280
I see. That's what he said, huh?

02:58.280 --> 02:59.180
Yeah.

03:01.820 --> 03:06.670
The recording session ended
before I knew what was happening. I...

03:06.670 --> 03:08.030
Syo-kun.

03:08.940 --> 03:14.340
I was really excited when
I heard your brother was an idol.

03:15.070 --> 03:17.530
Not only that, but I had the
opportunity to sing a duet with him.

03:17.530 --> 03:21.510
At first, I was surprised,
but then I was super excited.

03:21.510 --> 03:26.660
You were really looking forward
to singing with his brother.

03:26.660 --> 03:31.160
If we don't do our best
to perform fun songs and dances,

03:31.160 --> 03:34.060
our fans won't enjoy it, either.

03:36.490 --> 03:38.190
But...

03:38.790 --> 03:43.550
From the moment we met,
it was like he didn't care.

03:44.100 --> 03:47.080
He didn't say anything
during the meeting for the song.

03:47.080 --> 03:50.380
He's right. He didn't say anything
about his musical preferences

03:50.380 --> 03:52.790
or what he imagined the song would be like.

03:53.460 --> 03:57.380
But he sang it immediately
once I gave it to him.

03:57.380 --> 04:00.420
He even got the dance moves
the choreographer taught us

04:00.420 --> 04:03.400
right in one shot with perfect rhythm.

04:03.400 --> 04:06.360
That's right. His dancing was very powerful.

04:07.380 --> 04:11.400
So I thought he'd put just as
much passion towards the duet.

04:12.020 --> 04:14.440
But it's like he didn't even see me.

04:15.190 --> 04:18.150
I see. He hasn't changed at all.

04:19.570 --> 04:26.000
Since he was a child, he always challenged
me when it came to sports or games.

04:26.000 --> 04:28.830
But when it comes to anything else,
he's completely disinterested.

04:29.570 --> 04:32.040
He really hasn't changed.

04:32.350 --> 04:38.360
Damn it. I thought it'd be a great
song if he just sang a little harder.

04:38.910 --> 04:41.050
And he suddenly hit me, too.

04:44.230 --> 04:45.590
<i>Muscle Fight</i>...

04:46.910 --> 04:49.480
What's <i>Muscle Fight</i>?

04:49.480 --> 04:54.120
It's sports variety program that
pits celebrities against each other.

04:54.120 --> 05:01.280
Yeah. Powerful and agile celebrities
face off in a variety of contests on the show.

05:01.280 --> 05:06.340
At the end, the two highest-scoring
participants take each other on in a fight.

05:06.950 --> 05:10.050
Hyuga-sensei, have you been on the show?

05:10.050 --> 05:11.770
A long time ago.

05:11.770 --> 05:15.100
He was on the now-legendary first episode.

05:15.100 --> 05:17.210
He scored way more points than anyone else.

05:17.650 --> 05:21.770
On top of that, everyone who placed second
or lower forfeited the final battle.

05:21.770 --> 05:24.720
It was a total victory for Hyuga-sensei.

05:24.720 --> 05:26.350
That's amazing.

05:26.350 --> 05:27.470
Are you making another appearance?

05:27.470 --> 05:29.760
They extended me an offer
for the first time in a while.

05:32.050 --> 05:37.340
He said he'd go on <i>Muscle Fight</i>
to beat you, Hyuga-sensei.

05:40.530 --> 05:43.820
Will you let me appear on <i>Muscle Fight</i>?

05:45.940 --> 05:47.500
I want to beat him!

05:47.500 --> 05:50.870
I want to beat him,
so he'll sing with me again!

05:53.880 --> 05:54.950
Fine.

06:08.330 --> 06:09.570
Long time, no see.

06:09.570 --> 06:11.350
You look as composed as ever.

06:13.790 --> 06:15.770
I'm going to be on <i>Muscle Fight</i>, too.

06:16.680 --> 06:19.850
Prepare yourself.
I'm not the man I used to be.

06:21.260 --> 06:23.940
Kurusu will be appearing in my place.

06:23.940 --> 06:25.240
What?

06:25.240 --> 06:26.810
You're running from a fight?

06:28.390 --> 06:30.750
Don't just stand there! Say something!

06:32.350 --> 06:35.330
Why did you become an idol?

06:35.330 --> 06:38.670
What? I don't care about being an idol.

06:38.670 --> 06:42.710
I joined Raging Entertainment
so I could beat you.

06:43.780 --> 06:46.590
You're still going on about that?

06:46.590 --> 06:48.050
Of course.

06:50.350 --> 06:52.050
Kurusu is strong.

06:52.050 --> 06:54.220
That shrimp is strong?

06:54.220 --> 06:56.150
You'll see once you face him.

06:58.930 --> 07:00.150
Hey, wait!

07:04.130 --> 07:07.990
If I beat Kurusu, you'll fight me one-on-one.

07:08.870 --> 07:10.360
Very well.

07:13.990 --> 07:15.870
Have you been eating right?

07:15.870 --> 07:16.710
What?

07:17.450 --> 07:20.370
You should come home once in a while.

07:24.960 --> 07:29.210
Say your prayers, Hyuga Ryuya.

07:31.010 --> 07:33.470
Muscle Fight Contestant Announcement

07:37.560 --> 07:38.570
Hey.

07:39.150 --> 07:41.480
How dare you stick your nose in my business?

07:45.360 --> 07:46.520
Syo-kun.

07:46.520 --> 07:50.440
Listen up. If I win, you have
to sing our duet with me again.

07:51.390 --> 07:54.900
Fine. You're just the opening act.

07:54.900 --> 07:56.620
Beating you will be a piece of cake.

08:00.730 --> 08:01.620
Eight.

08:03.740 --> 08:04.540
Nine.

08:06.650 --> 08:07.370
Ten.

08:12.050 --> 08:15.460
You did five whole sets today. That's amazing.

08:16.180 --> 08:19.170
At this rate, you'll reach a hundred sets soon.

08:19.170 --> 08:21.190
W-What kind of math is that?

08:21.190 --> 08:22.390
It's all right.

08:23.190 --> 08:25.060
I know you can do it, Syo-chan.

08:40.100 --> 08:40.770
Syo.

08:40.770 --> 08:42.750
Hey, shorty. You're working hard.

08:43.810 --> 08:45.360
What are you guys doing here?

08:45.360 --> 08:46.740
You're no fun.

08:46.740 --> 08:47.830
Here.

08:49.660 --> 08:54.200
Nanami told us you're fighting
Hyuga Yamato on <i>Muscle Fight</i>.

08:54.200 --> 08:55.840
Do your best.

08:55.840 --> 08:57.220
Yeah, thanks.

08:58.450 --> 09:00.150
It's finally tomorrow.

09:00.150 --> 09:01.140
Indeed.

09:01.560 --> 09:04.130
His opponent is HEAVENS' power fighter.

09:04.130 --> 09:06.250
It won't be easy.

09:06.250 --> 09:08.250
They'll be fighting one-on-one.

09:08.250 --> 09:10.770
All we can do is watch over him.

09:10.770 --> 09:13.150
But he'll be fine.

09:13.540 --> 09:14.500
You're right.

09:17.070 --> 09:18.160
Thanks.

09:18.160 --> 09:20.900
Sorry for asking you to rewrite the song.

09:20.900 --> 09:21.700
It's fine.

09:21.700 --> 09:25.370
I have a feeling we can sing
something more passionate.

09:27.320 --> 09:29.380
He's really amazing, you know?

09:30.040 --> 09:32.390
He showed me that
so many times during practice.

09:32.910 --> 09:34.570
He's not just built.

09:34.570 --> 09:38.680
His dance moves are exceptional,
and his singing voice is smooth, too.

09:39.390 --> 09:40.970
Syo-kun.

09:42.260 --> 09:47.800
But if he's only an idol because
of his rivalry with Hyuga-sensei,

09:49.130 --> 09:50.980
then he's not a real idol.

10:06.990 --> 10:07.710
Okay.

10:09.490 --> 10:11.180
Come watch the show.

10:11.180 --> 10:16.050
I'll knock him out
so he has to sing with me again.

10:16.590 --> 10:17.420
I will.

10:18.510 --> 10:23.310
I want to make everyone
smile by singing your song.

10:40.650 --> 10:43.240
What are all of you doing here?

10:43.240 --> 10:47.410
The duet project involves all of STARISH.

10:48.830 --> 10:50.440
You just wait.

10:50.440 --> 10:54.200
I'll pass the baton Tokiya
gave me onto the next guy.

10:54.610 --> 10:57.630
We have to make the Duet Project a success.

10:57.630 --> 10:59.170
Of course.

11:00.510 --> 11:01.480
Yeah!

11:03.650 --> 11:05.390
It's finally time to start

11:05.390 --> 11:09.060
the Celebrity sports variety program
"Muscle Fight!"

11:09.060 --> 11:14.650
Tonight under the full moon, who will
become the number one sports celebrity?

11:14.650 --> 11:17.530
You won't be able to take your eyes off them.

11:20.790 --> 11:23.830
As usual, the first competition
is the stone jump.

11:23.830 --> 11:25.600
Competitors will cross the lake
by jumping on the stones

11:25.600 --> 11:29.120
and are scored according to the order
in which they arrive on the opposite side.

11:29.120 --> 11:31.450
It's as simple as it looks.

11:31.450 --> 11:34.940
However, agility, jumping ability,
core strength, and balance, as well as

11:34.940 --> 11:38.670
the ability to identify which stones to jump on
and the guts to actually do it are all tested

11:38.670 --> 11:43.230
in this truly perfect contest
that mustn't be underestimated.

11:44.930 --> 11:47.780
The competitors are already
standing at the starting line.

11:47.780 --> 11:50.520
Who will win the first contest?

11:53.320 --> 11:55.370
The starting signal marks the beginning

11:55.370 --> 11:59.570
of the competition and
rings throughout the stadium!

12:02.670 --> 12:04.390
Start!

12:07.610 --> 12:09.630
Kurusu is in danger!

12:09.630 --> 12:12.120
Is he dropping out already?

12:16.280 --> 12:18.370
He managed to regain his balance.

12:19.500 --> 12:23.180
Several of the stones aren't fixed in
place, so the competitors must be careful.

12:27.410 --> 12:28.180
What are you doing?

12:28.840 --> 12:31.220
The battle has already begun.

12:36.730 --> 12:38.110
Goal!

12:39.480 --> 12:41.330
Hyuga Yamato is the first to cross.

12:41.330 --> 12:43.740
He showed us some powerful jumps.

12:44.470 --> 12:46.480
Kurusu Syo is the second to cross.

12:46.480 --> 12:48.660
He finished just after Hyuga,

12:48.660 --> 12:52.450
but he demonstrated an impressive
leaping charge with his nimble sense of balance.

12:53.000 --> 12:54.540
Good work.

12:57.130 --> 13:07.090
Hyuga Yamato

12:57.130 --> 13:07.090
Kurusu Syo

12:57.130 --> 13:07.090
Nakagami Keisuke

12:57.130 --> 13:07.090
Aida Daiki

12:58.010 --> 13:00.460
Hyuga Yamato receives ten points for first place.

13:00.460 --> 13:02.660
Kurusu Syo receives eight points for second.

13:02.660 --> 13:06.380
The remaining competitors
receive six, four, and two points each.

13:08.190 --> 13:14.600
Kurusu and Hyuga are scoring
tons of points in their respective specialties!

13:14.600 --> 13:16.650
Hyuga Yamato

13:14.600 --> 13:16.650
Kurusu Syo

13:15.390 --> 13:18.980
Neither one is giving any ground!

13:21.940 --> 13:24.580
We're in the final stage of the competition.

13:24.580 --> 13:27.790
Punches and kicks are allowed
in this all-out battle.

13:27.790 --> 13:30.120
Competitors who send their
opponents down for a count of ten

13:30.120 --> 13:34.290
or knock them out of the ring
will receive twenty points.

13:34.610 --> 13:39.130
These two competitors with
contrasting styles have risen to the stage.

13:39.130 --> 13:42.130
He may be small,
but he's surprised us countless times

13:42.130 --> 13:46.300
with his balance, agility, and boldness.

13:46.300 --> 13:48.610
The leaping charge he showed us during

13:48.610 --> 13:51.270
the stone jump was worthy of
a modern-day Ushiwakamaru.

13:51.270 --> 13:53.720
He's Kurusu Syo!

13:53.720 --> 13:57.180
On the other side is a man with
a large build, powerful movements,

13:57.180 --> 14:00.580
and an unbreakable will.

14:00.580 --> 14:06.370
With the intensity of Benkei,
he lets no man pass.

14:06.370 --> 14:08.320
He's Hyuga Yamato!

14:08.970 --> 14:11.730
We're at the Gojo Ohashi Bridge of this battle.

14:11.730 --> 14:13.830
Will he pass or won't he?

14:13.830 --> 14:17.850
Who will the goddess of victory smile upon?

14:19.100 --> 14:21.130
Ready, go!

14:22.540 --> 14:25.300
What's this? Kurusu strikes first!

14:25.690 --> 14:27.090
Strike first to win!

14:31.370 --> 14:34.430
Your kicks have no power!

14:37.770 --> 14:43.020
What's this? Hyuga has easily tossed
Kurusu aside with his powerful arms!

14:44.890 --> 14:47.360
Hyuga strikes out with a fierce low hit!

14:50.470 --> 14:52.620
Hyuga lets loose a raging rush of blows!

14:53.240 --> 14:55.540
Kurusu can't do anything but defend!

14:56.910 --> 14:59.120
Quit scurrying around!

14:59.810 --> 15:01.500
A left straight!

15:05.370 --> 15:08.070
A fierce blow from Hyuga!

15:08.070 --> 15:10.470
He blasted him with his powerful arms!

15:11.090 --> 15:13.810
Kurusu is paralyzed on the mat.

15:14.380 --> 15:16.710
You finally stopped moving.

15:18.230 --> 15:21.250
What's this? Kurusu is getting up.

15:21.250 --> 15:24.770
But he's wobbling back and forth.

15:25.340 --> 15:27.180
Is he all right?

15:27.890 --> 15:29.070
You still want to fight?

15:29.070 --> 15:30.910
Of course.

15:30.910 --> 15:32.470
He's back in a fighting stance!

15:32.470 --> 15:34.240
The match will resume!

15:36.410 --> 15:38.410
Oh, really?

15:39.000 --> 15:41.330
Hyuga closes the distance
in the blink of an eye!

15:44.200 --> 15:47.250
He's attacking Kurusu
with a raging flurry of blows!

15:49.650 --> 15:52.010
Kurusu is on his knees again!

15:53.000 --> 15:56.200
Will the match end like this?

16:01.880 --> 16:03.810
You're next.

16:05.950 --> 16:07.230
Wait.

16:07.670 --> 16:10.030
Kurusu is getting up.

16:10.780 --> 16:14.700
I'm your opponent.

16:15.810 --> 16:18.700
Just stay down already!

16:18.700 --> 16:21.350
Hyuga unleashes a series of raging blows.

16:21.350 --> 16:23.580
Is the fight over?

16:25.700 --> 16:27.290
You never give up.

16:28.890 --> 16:32.280
You don't seem to get it yet.

16:32.280 --> 16:33.260
What?

16:37.350 --> 16:39.560
Don't underestimate an idol.

16:40.950 --> 16:44.850
I won't lose to someone as half-assed as you!

16:44.850 --> 16:48.190
Those are big words
for someone as ragged as you.

16:51.290 --> 17:01.790
Syo! Syo! Syo!

16:55.110 --> 16:56.960
They're awfully noisy.

16:56.960 --> 16:58.910
It won't change the fact
that I'm going to win.

17:00.340 --> 17:01.790
Why are you smiling?

17:01.790 --> 17:05.040
You really don't get it.

17:05.040 --> 17:06.080
What?

17:06.420 --> 17:11.050
I'll show you what
an idol's spirit looks like!

17:11.880 --> 17:15.930
You don't even have
the strength left to move!

17:21.720 --> 17:23.890
Wh-What's going on?

17:23.890 --> 17:25.940
An idol...

17:32.330 --> 17:40.030
Makes everyone smile,
and carries the burden of those smiles!

17:51.910 --> 17:54.290
Carries the burden of those smiles?

18:07.740 --> 18:11.480
Let's keep fighting, Hyuga Yamato.

18:11.480 --> 18:14.940
Of course, Kurusu Syo!

18:33.420 --> 18:39.590
If you don't know what to do with your
frozen heart, I'll punch and shout at you

18:39.590 --> 18:45.680
Pushing the excited blood
in your veins into motion

18:46.010 --> 18:51.730
Overflowing with passion,
let's go beyond together

18:52.060 --> 18:58.110
The depths of our eyes won't stop glittering

18:58.110 --> 19:02.660
Let's go! Take this!

19:01.240 --> 19:05.230
Hurry up! Come on!

19:05.230 --> 19:07.020
I'm so excited

19:07.020 --> 19:08.540
Come and attack me

19:08.540 --> 19:14.090
In our passionate battle

19:14.090 --> 19:17.300
Come on and burn! (Burn!) Burn! (Burn!)

19:17.300 --> 19:20.550
The shine (Shine!) illuminating us
(Shine!) in this dark night burns

19:20.550 --> 19:22.220
Is that all you've got?

19:22.220 --> 19:23.550
Don't be absurd

19:23.550 --> 19:26.720
Go beyond the JUSTICE IMPULSE

19:26.720 --> 19:29.850
Rush! (Rush!) Rush! (Rush!)

19:29.850 --> 19:32.730
Kick! (Kick!) Kick (Kick!)
your own shadows aside

19:32.730 --> 19:34.480
With all your strength

19:34.480 --> 19:36.230
Come at me

19:36.230 --> 19:41.700
The curtains have risen

19:41.700 --> 19:44.950
On a new energy

19:44.950 --> 19:46.830
Two sources of passion

19:46.830 --> 19:48.220
When they rise

19:48.220 --> 19:49.370
Big Bang

20:08.720 --> 20:12.350
You heard our song, right?

20:14.480 --> 20:19.220
Wasn't it so passionate and awesome?

20:20.040 --> 20:23.310
That was just a hallucination.

20:26.550 --> 20:27.950
Syo-chan!

20:27.950 --> 20:29.710
Yamato!

20:29.710 --> 20:31.160
You can do it!

20:38.020 --> 20:42.550
Don't you want everyone to hear our song?

20:43.220 --> 20:46.180
Look at how much they support us.

20:46.180 --> 20:47.950
They're just loud.

20:50.520 --> 20:52.600
You're not very honest.

20:56.680 --> 20:59.890
It's a double knockout!

21:34.890 --> 21:36.140
Hey, Yamato!

21:36.590 --> 21:38.770
I'll be waiting for you
in the studio tomorrow!

21:43.780 --> 21:46.020
Syo-chan, are you okay?

21:46.530 --> 21:48.670
Natsuki? You came?

21:48.670 --> 21:52.150
Yeah. I was watching from
the guest seats with Haru-chan.

21:53.580 --> 21:54.410
Nanami.

21:54.410 --> 21:56.060
Are you okay?

21:56.060 --> 21:58.050
Yeah, I'm totally fine.

21:58.050 --> 21:58.790
Ow!

21:59.410 --> 22:01.860
Syo-chan, where does it hurt?

22:01.860 --> 22:04.050
Ow! Don't grab my face!

22:05.290 --> 22:09.100
It wasn't a very good fight, though.

22:09.850 --> 22:11.760
That's not true.

22:12.070 --> 22:13.060
Really?

22:19.440 --> 22:23.230
But now I get to sing
that song with him again.

22:23.230 --> 22:24.360
Yeah.

24:05.960 --> 24:07.710
I'm glad we got to meet again.

24:07.710 --> 24:09.550
Don't take your eyes off me.

24:09.550 --> 24:10.970
Uta Pri!
